# escape_geaga -- Géaga at the Well of Segais: she sees the ghost, and all its forebears behind it; it asks to go back
# to the living; she refuses (the law of the well), then looks away from the north stair.
# Plays as you wake at the well (the scene opens it); talk to her again afterwards and you get the last node only.
# The card of her turning sets escape_geaga_blind_eye: her roots across the north stair part.

@file underworld/escape
@encounter 0

= she wakes: never one
@when !note escape_geaga_blind_eye
@continue
I see thee, champion. I see thee, and the one before thee,
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
and all of them stretching back and back into the dark.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
Thou art a flowering of that old root.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
Thou art come to where all things that were, are still.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= the asking
@when !note escape_geaga_blind_eye
@continue
Back.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
Thou wouldst go back up into the green world,
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
to walk again where the rain falls and fires are lit against the dark.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
It is an old asking. I have heard it before.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
What comes down into the dark does not go back up into the light.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= she looks away
@when !note escape_geaga_blind_eye
@note escape_geaga_blind_eye
She says no more.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
Slowly, as a tree turns from the wind, she turns her eyes from the north stair.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= afterwards
@when note escape_geaga_blind_eye
She says nothing. She is not looking.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
